# Biblical Hebrew speech dictionary for Dutch TTS (Tiberian/Erasmian pronunciation).
# Transliterates pointed Hebrew into Dutch-phonetic text before speech.
# Fields: pattern<TAB>replacement<TAB>caseSensitive<TAB>type
# type 0 = ANYWHERE (literal), type 1 = REGEXP.
# Order matters: regex strips and reorder rules must precede literal substitutions.

# ====================================================================
# Section 1: Strip cantillation marks and direction characters.
# Removes the extended cantillation range that liblouis discards
# (hbo-ihbc-rules.uti:51), keeping only atnach, zaqef qatan,
# sof pasuq, and maqaf for later punctuation mapping.
# ====================================================================
[\u0592\u0593\u0595-\u05A1\u05A3-\u05AD\u05BD\u05BF]		0	1
[\u200E\u200F\u202D\u202E]		0	1

# ====================================================================
# Section 2: Dagesh reorder for BKP consonants (regex, type 1).
# Moves dagesh from after the letter (with any niqqud in between)
# to immediately before the letter, so Section 6 literal rules can
# match dagesh+letter directly. Mirrors hbo-common-rules.uti:58.
# Five rules: bet, kaf, kaf-sofit, pe, pe-sofit.
# ====================================================================
(ב)([\u05B0-\u05BB\u05C7]*)ּ	ּ\1\2	0	1
(כ)([\u05B0-\u05BB\u05C7]*)ּ	ּ\1\2	0	1
(ך)([\u05B0-\u05BB\u05C7]*)ּ	ּ\1\2	0	1
(פ)([\u05B0-\u05BB\u05C7]*)ּ	ּ\1\2	0	1
(ף)([\u05B0-\u05BB\u05C7]*)ּ	ּ\1\2	0	1

# ====================================================================
# Section 3: Shin/sin dot normalization (literal, type 0).
# Must precede bare-shin fallback in Section 7.
# ====================================================================
שׁ	sh	0	0
שׂ	s	0	0

# ====================================================================
# Section 4: Matres lectionis — vowel + silent letter (literal, type 0).
# Two-character long-vowel combinations where the second character
# is silent. Must precede single-char consonant rules for vav/yod.
# ====================================================================
וֹ	o	0	0
וּ	oe	0	0
ֵי	e	0	0
ִי	ie	0	0
ֹי	o	0	0

# ====================================================================
# Section 5: Sheva disambiguation (regex, type 1).
# Must fire before consonants are substituted.
# Rules ordered most-specific first.
# Rule 1: double sheva — first silent, second vocal (drop first, keep second as e).
# Rule 2: word-final sheva — silent (not followed by Hebrew letter or niqqud).
# Rule 3: closed-syllable sheva after short vowel — silent.
# Rule 4 (fallback): remaining sheva handled as 'e' in Section 8.
# ====================================================================
([\u05D0-\u05EA])ְ([\u05D0-\u05EA])ְ	\1\2e	0	1
ְ(?![\u0591-\u05C7\u05D0-\u05EA])		0	1
([ִֶַֻ])([\u05D0-\u05EA])ְ	\1\2	0	1

# ====================================================================
# Section 6: Dagesh + BKP consonants (post-reorder form, literal, type 0).
# After Section 2 the dagesh sits immediately before the consonant.
# Tav is omitted here (no alternation per user decision).
# Final rule strips any stray dagesh (on gimel, dalet, tav, etc.).
# ====================================================================
ּב	b	0	0
ּכ	k	0	0
ּך	k	0	0
ּפ	p	0	0
ּף	p	0	0
ּ		0	0

# ====================================================================
# Section 7: Consonants (single chars, including final/sofit forms).
# ====================================================================
א	'	0	0
ב	v	0	0
ג	g	0	0
ד	d	0	0
ה	h	0	0
ו	w	0	0
ז	z	0	0
ח	ch	0	0
ט	t	0	0
י	j	0	0
כ	ch	0	0
ך	ch	0	0
ל	l	0	0
מ	m	0	0
ם	m	0	0
נ	n	0	0
ן	n	0	0
ס	s	0	0
ע	'	0	0
פ	f	0	0
ף	f	0	0
צ	ts	0	0
ץ	ts	0	0
ק	k	0	0
ר	r	0	0
ש	sh	0	0
ת	t	0	0

# ====================================================================
# Section 8: Vowel points (niqqud, literal, type 0).
# Sheva fallback here handles any vocal sheva not caught by Section 5.
# ====================================================================
ְ	e	0	0
ַ	a	0	0
ָ	aa	0	0
ׇ	o	0	0
ֶ	e	0	0
ֵ	e	0	0
ִ	ie	0	0
ֹ	o	0	0
ֻ	oe	0	0
ֱ	e	0	0
ֲ	a	0	0
ֳ	o	0	0
ֺ	o	0	0

# ====================================================================
# Section 9: Accents → punctuation (literal, type 0).
# In-place replacement; exact word position not needed for TTS pausing.
# atnach (U+0591) → semicolon, zaqef qatan (U+0594) → comma,
# sof pasuq (U+05C3) → period, maqaf (U+05BE) → hyphen.
# ====================================================================
֑	;	0	0
֔	,	0	0
׃	.	0	0
־	-	0	0

# ====================================================================
# Section 10: Miscellaneous Hebrew punctuation (literal, type 0).
# Paseq (U+05C0) stripped (word-internal separator, not needed for TTS).
# Gershayim and geresh (abbreviation marks) left untouched.
# ====================================================================
׀		0	0
